    "topic": "Probability",
    "difficulty": "Standard",
    "isSketch": false,
    "statement": "Two buses, M and Z, arrive at fixed minutes past each hour, with one of each bus every hour. You arrive at a uniformly distributed random time and observe that you are much more likely to catch bus M than bus Z. Given that bus Z arrives during the first half of the hour ($0 < z \\le 30$), what can you deduce about arrival times $m$ and $z$?",
