    "statement": "Consider a set of ten positive integers $S = \\{x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_{10}\\}$ with $0 < x_i < 100$. Prove that there exist two distinct subsets of $S$ that have the exact same sum. What affects the likelihood: the range or the number of elements?",
